# Field, every kind, in every state: six pictures of one tree — the resting one, and one
# per `State`.
#
# The rows are the five states `snapshot` accepts, plus the rest that has no
# variant to name it. The columns are `Background`, `Foreground`, `Border`,
# `Opacity` and `Shadow`, then all five at once, then the control that answers
# to nothing — so a picture says which element responded and how, with the cell
# that did not beside the ones that did.
#
# Six kinds, and the scene names each of them — the `type` the markup carries,
# or `multiline` for the `textarea` that has none. **The password row is the one
# that paints differently**: its value is one bullet per character, never the
# word, which is what a browser draws for `<input type="password">`. The other
# five are deliberately identical, and so are a browser's once `appearance:none`
# has taken the chrome it would tell them apart by; one of the five that stopped
# matching its neighbours is the finding. The second difference a browser keeps
# — only a `textarea` wraps — needs a value longer than this picture's and is
# pinned in `cli/runtime/paint.rs`.
#
# That row is why the scene carries the kind at all. Until buri#89 closed,
# `describe` dropped it, all six painted alike, and a `buri test --update` on a
# suite that snapshots a password field wrote the secret into a file somebody
# commits.
#
# The sheet resets `:where(input:not([type=checkbox]),textarea)` to the same
# control reset a button gets, which is why no `Focus` picture here carries a
# browser focus ring: a ring is the `border` and `shadow` columns or nothing.
#
# `:checked` is the one a browser would never fire on a text input — a checkbox
# is a toggle here, never a field — and the painter fires it anyway, because a
# snapshot's state is the whole tree's.
#
# The negative twin moves one number in one cell of the hover palette. Exactly
# one of the six goldens changes, which is what the state pictures rest on:
# they are six documents, not six copies of one.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs.

doc: "every `FieldKind` answering to every state, five properties to a column, with the border and the inner shadow the sheet resets, painted and compared against six goldens with the whole record-and-fail lifecycle over them"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/field", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/field/test/__snapshots__/field-resting.diff.png"  exists: false }

# A snapshot nobody has recorded yet says how to record one.
edit {
  file: "lib/field/test/states.buri"
  replace: "snapshot(ctx, \"field-resting\""
  with: "snapshot(ctx, \"never-recorded\""
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/field", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "missing.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/field/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: false }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/field", "--update", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "recorded.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/field/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: true }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/field", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "again.txt"
}

# One number in the hover palette, and only the hover picture moves.
edit {
  file: "lib/field/scenes.buri"
  replace: ".Background(.Rgb(214, 44, 44))"
  with: ".Background(.Rgb(214, 44, 84))"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/field", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "changed.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/field/test/__snapshots__/field-hover.diff.png"  exists: true }
path { path: "lib/field/test/__snapshots__/field-focus.diff.png"  exists: false }
